// Secrets.example.xcconfig
//
// Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` (which is gitignored) and fill in the
// real value. NEVER commit `Secrets.xcconfig` — this repo is public.
//
// APP_KEY is the shared secret the backend requires as the `X-App-Key` header
// on every request. It MUST match the `APP_KEY` set in the backend's .env /
// Railway environment. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
//
// One-time Xcode wiring (per target that talks to the backend — the app and,
// if it makes requests, the Share Extension):
//   1. Add Secrets.xcconfig to the project in Xcode (File > Add Files…).
//   2. Project > Info > Configurations: set Secrets.xcconfig as the base
//      configuration for Debug and Release (or `#include` it from an existing
//      base xcconfig).
// The build setting `INFOPLIST_KEY_APP_KEY = $(APP_KEY)` (already in the target
// build settings) then injects this value into the generated Info.plist, where
// RecipeKit's AppConfig reads it at runtime.

APP_KEY = replace-with-a-real-secret
